{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg --files .pose/specs | rg review-readiness; cat .pose/workflows/review.md .pose/rules/security.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md .pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md; git diff --stat 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2; pose context --task spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal --json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg --files .pose/specs | rg review-readiness; cat .pose/workflows/review.md .pose/rules/security.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md .pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md; git diff --stat 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2; pose context --task spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal --json'","aggregated_output":".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n# Workflow: Review\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that a change is correct, production-safe, and aligned with its approved scope and specs.\n\n## Preconditions\n\n- Make the final diff readable through cohesive commits or batches.\n- Provide requirement and spec context.\n- Attach implementer validation evidence, including `pose validate` output.\n- Define acceptance criteria and expected risk.\n\n## Execution checklist\n\n1. Resolve `pose review bundle <scope> --explain` (or `pose_review_bundle`) when bundle policy is enabled; otherwise resolve `pose review-plan <scope> --explain`.\n2. Confirm the semantic scope, patch/tree identity, mapped components and bundle plan digest.\n3. Run required active tools first, evaluate recommended tools explicitly and leave completion-only tools deferred until an attestation exists.\n4. Select the plan's applicable rules explicitly and record them in the review.\n5. Resolve rule conflicts with the most restrictive option, prioritizing security for exposure, authorization, and integrity risks.\n6. Consult `.pose/knowledge/` for relevant handoffs, accepted risks, follow-ups, and decision logs.\n7. Check compliance with specs, contracts, and local instructions.\n8. Review functional correctness and edge cases.\n9. Evaluate security, observability, and performance risks.\n10. Require validation evidence from `.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json` proportional to risk.\n11. Identify regression and rollout or rollback risks.\n12. Run plan-selected assessments, including tech-debt and integration when applicable.\n13. Classify findings by severity and propose objective actions.\n14. **Produce a handoff** in `.pose/knowledge/` when findings result in accepted risk, post-merge monitoring, or deferred work (`pose new-knowledge handoff <slug>`); link it from the review.\n15. Seal the validated subject with `pose review bundle <scope> --seal`; stop if any input is unclassified or changed since preparation.\n16. Issue a final decision: approved, approved with reservations, changes requested, or rejected.\n17. Record the decision with `pose review attest <bundle-id> ... --plan-digest <sha256> --apply`; signed external envelopes use `pose review attest --envelope <path> --apply`.\n18. Run `pose review verify <scope>` and `pose review-check <scope>`; reject stale, incomplete, conflicting or transitively invalid reused criteria.\n19. Apply closeout only after verification reports `ready-to-close`; lifecycle, state and report refreshes must not change the sealed bundle.\n20. When Contributor Mode is active and review identifies linter false-positives, diagnostic frictions, or POSE rule gaps, stage an improvement proposal via `pose contribute stage --type enhancement`.\n\n## Required rule selection\n\nAttach this section to the review:\n\n```md\n## Rules applied during review\n- Change type: <feature|bugfix|refactor|documentation-update|mixed>\n- Workflow consulted: `.pose/workflows/<file>.md`\n- Rules selected:\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/security.md`\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` (extension `pose-rule-backend-go`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/frontend-react.md` (extension `pose-rule-frontend-react`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/kubernetes.md` (extension `pose-rule-kubernetes`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md` when knowledge or process changes\n- Rationale for each selected rule: <one line per item>\n- Rules not applicable: <list and explain>\n```\n\n## Recurrence escalation\n\n- Trigger `.pose/workflows/recurrence-escalation.md` when recurring rework is uncovered and the threshold is met.\n- Require `recurrence_rework_uncovered` evidence for the 30-day period.\n- Require explicit links from the specialized workflow to applicable domain rules.\n- Require a formal keep, adjust, or discard decision after the 45-day pilot.\n\n## Minimum domain coverage\n\n- React UI: apply `frontend-react`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Go services: apply `backend-go`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Cluster deployment or infrastructure: apply `kubernetes`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Process, spec, workflow, rule, or report: apply `documentation-style`, `knowledge-governance`, and security when sensitive data is involved.\n- Cross-stack changes: apply every touched domain rule cumulatively.\n\n## Domain review checklist\n\n### Security\n\n- Confirm authentication, authorization, and least privilege when applicable.\n- Verify that code, configuration, manifests, docs, and logs contain no secrets.\n- Require applicable vulnerability and secret-scanning evidence.\n\n### Contracts\n\n- Confirm compatibility of public HTTP, event, schema, CLI, and file contracts.\n- Validate forward and backward compatibility for rollout and rollback.\n- Require a spec update for contract changes.\n\n### Observability\n\n- Verify structured logs and metrics without sensitive data.\n- Confirm that probes, health checks, and alerts reflect real behavior.\n- Preserve enough traceability for post-deployment diagnosis.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Require lint, typecheck, test, and build coverage proportional to risk.\n- Require executed `pose validate` evidence and relevant results.\n- Record environment limitations and residual validation risks.\n\n## Editorial checklist\n\n- Use imperative, actionable instructions.\n- Keep bullets short and avoid duplicated sections.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- Reference explicit files and paths.\n\n## Required outputs\n\n- A review decision with rationale.\n- The inspected effective plan, its component provenance and tool dispositions.\n- An immutable sealed review bundle and separate attestation bound to its exact digest.\n- A completed rule-selection section.\n- Findings with severity, evidence, and recommendation.\n- Recurrence classification by domain and cause with preventive actions.\n- An explicit statement about public contracts and compatibility.\n- Residual risks and safe-deployment conditions.\n- References to executed checks and collected evidence.\n\n## Complete multi-rule review example\n\n```md\n## Review Summary\n- Decision: approved with reservations\n- Change type: feature (Go API, React UI, and Helm)\n- Workflow: `.pose/workflows/feature.md`\n\n## Rules applied during review\n- `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` (extension `pose-rule-backend-go`): verified handlers, context, and error handling.\n- `.pose/rules/frontend-react.md` (extension `pose-rule-frontend-react`): verified accessibility and explicit loading and error states.\n- `.pose/rules/kubernetes.md` (extension `pose-rule-kubernetes`): verified resources, probes, and immutable images.\n- `.pose/rules/security.md`: verified authorization and absence of secrets.\n- `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`: verified editorial consistency.\n\n## Checks and evidence\n- `pose validate`: passed\n- `go test ./...`: passed in the backend module\n- `pnpm lint && pnpm test`: passed in the frontend module\n- `helm template` and `kubectl apply --dry-run=client`: passed\n\n## Contracts and compatibility\n- Preserved `POST /v1/storage`.\n- Added optional `retentionDays`, preserving backward compatibility.\n\n## Findings\n- Medium: missing queue-saturation alert; add a metric and alert before production.\n- Low: frontend error lacks request-id context; improve observable UX.\n\n## Residual risks\n- Review did not simulate real cluster load.\n- Increase monitoring during the first 24 hours.\n```\n\n## CI failure interpretation\n\n- Treat `POSE check (strict)` as merge-blocking on protected branches.\n- Treat failed required checks in `POSE validate (strict)` as merge-blocking.\n- Attach pipeline artifacts: `pose-check.log`, `pose-validate.latest.log`, and the POSE report.\n- Classify optional-check failures as quality reservations with an owned remediation plan.\n- Reject changes that violate specs, public contracts, security, or safe rollout.\n\n## Phased rollout for unready modules\n\n- Enforce the current required checks immediately.\n- Use `moduleOverrides` to phase adoption without weakening global structural and required gates.\n- Promote optional checks to required by module with an owner and agreed window.\n\n### Optional-to-required promotion protocol\n\n- Select a pilot domain and map candidate checks with owners and explicit risks.\n- Measure success for four weeks and require a baseline of at least 95 percent.\n- Promote only eligible domains through `moduleOverrides`.\n- Update the validation matrix and quality policy in the same change set.\n- Monitor regressions and adjust rollout without removing established required gates.\n- Update specs and rules when rollout changes merge acceptance criteria.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Resolve or formally accept every critical and high finding.\n- Make the final decision clear and actionable.\n- Support quality and security conclusions with evidence.\n- Preserve approved scope without unjustified drift.\n\n## Reviewer mode\n\n**Objective:** evaluate technical quality and production readiness with emphasis on correctness, risk, and scope.\n\n- **Focus:** functional correctness, spec consistency, regression and security risk, operability, validation quality, and actionable feedback.\n- **Anti-patterns:** approve without sufficient evidence; review style while ignoring functional risk; request unrelated changes; block progress on subjective preference.\n- **Handoff:** state the decision, severity and evidence for each finding, safe merge or deployment conditions, accepted risks, and recommended monitoring.\n# Rule: Security\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for authentication, authorization, sensitive data, external integrations, dependencies, and attack surfaces.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Apply least privilege to resource and credential access.\n- Store secrets only in appropriate secret-management mechanisms, never in code.\n- Validate and sanitize external input for its execution context.\n- Keep personal and confidential data out of plaintext logs and metrics.\n- Evaluate new dependencies for maintenance, licensing, and known vulnerabilities.\n- Test both positive and negative authentication and authorization cases.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Committing credentials, tokens, keys, or secrets in any versioned artifact.\n- Disabling TLS or certificate verification without a formally documented mitigation.\n- Trusting client input for authorization decisions.\n- Executing dynamic commands without adequate validation and escaping.\n- Ignoring critical security alerts without an approved exception record.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run secret scanning on the changed diff or scope.\n- Run the module's applicable dependency vulnerability scanner.\n- Pass the relevant authentication and authorization tests.\n- Complete a review for sensitive-data exposure in logs and configuration.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Delivery Evidence\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when writing or reviewing any document that **claims delivery,\ncompletion, or readiness**: status reports, handoffs, summaries, module READMEs,\ncurrent-state sections in specs or proposals, and messages that say something is complete.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Claim delivery only with attached, verifiable gate evidence: command and output\n  (`pose validate`, `go test`, `tsc`, `vitest`) or a link to the corresponding POSE report.\n- Use POSE lifecycle vocabulary: `draft`, `in-progress`, `done`, `blocked`,\n  `superseded`, or `abandoned`. Do not invent labels such as `completed` or `100% COMPLETE`.\n- Separate **implemented and verified** work from **planned or documented** work.\n  A plan describes intent; do not present that intent as current reality.\n- Reference the report or evidence that crossed the spec exit gate before using `done`.\n- Convert relative dates to absolute dates and stamp the verification date.\n- Declare exact source-tree artifact actions in the spec and reconcile them\n  against an immutable Git change set before claiming delivery.\n- Treat artifact declarations, Git observations and delivery verification as\n  separate evidence; none proves the others by itself.\n- For typed delivery targets, require a path from reconciled artifacts through\n  a production entrypoint to current structured validation results. A surface\n  requires reachability plus integration/e2e evidence; a composed capability\n  requires integration evidence.\n- Evidence answers for the component it ran in or for a component inside it: a\n  module-wide run covers its subtree, but a result from a directory inside a\n  component does not answer for the whole component. Coverage that rests only\n  on a containing module is reported as `inferred-coverage` — name it as such.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Claiming `100% COMPLETE` or production readiness without a green\n  `pose validate --strict` for every affected module.\n- Publishing contradictory delivery documents for the same scope; reconcile them first.\n- Merging code with completion documentation before the applicable POSE checks pass.\n- Mixing aspiration and verified state in one paragraph without clear labels.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `pose check --strict` for structure and spec status enums.\n- Run `pose validate --strict` for every module the document claims to deliver.\n- Run `pose lint-spec` when the document is a spec.\n- Run `pose artifact-check --strict` when the scope changes governed source-tree paths.\n- Run `pose surface-check --strict` for specs with `delivers` and `pose\n  roadmap-check --strict` before a roadmap claims completion.\n- `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` when closing specs to update completeness metrics, technical debt, and reports under `.pose/assessments/` and `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence over progress narratives when rules conflict.\n- When pressured to claim completion without a gate, record the real state\n  (`in-progress` or `blocked`) and the remaining exit conditions.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n .../adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md |   31 +\n .pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json              | 3418 ++++++++++++++------\n .pose/indexes/generation.json                      |   16 +-\n .pose/indexes/spec-graph.json                      | 1284 ++++----\n .pose/results/delivery-validation.json             | 1396 ++++----\n .pose/results/review-readiness-binding.md          |    1 +\n ...23-pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone.md |  110 +\n ...2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md |  110 +\n ...2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md |  167 +\n ...11-23-pose-review-subject-includes-its-index.md |  110 +\n ...1-23-pose-run-verification-pins-brief-inputs.md |  110 +\n ...-validate-carry-report-and-closeout-coverage.md |  110 +\n ...23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md |  109 +\n POSE.md                                            |    4 +-\n locales/pt-BR/POSE.md                              |    4 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go                  |    5 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go              |    1 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go           |    2 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go           |   23 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go        |   92 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go   |  123 +\n .../internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go     |   62 +\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/live_policy_reads_test.go   |    2 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go             |   29 +-\n .../pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go     |   20 +-\n .../pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go        |    2 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go        |    2 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go            |   12 +\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go          |   11 +\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go       |  114 +\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go    |   49 +\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure_test.go    |   21 +\n .../testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json    |    3 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md            |    4 +-\n .../internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md   |    4 +-\n 35 files changed, 5246 insertions(+), 2315 deletions(-)\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"selected_project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n  \"selected_revision\": \"62a4e0f2730713ccd2913075ff980041c189f2c6\",\n  \"task_ref\": \"xref:proj.pose-dist/spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal\",\n  \"authority\": {\n    \"project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n    \"kind\": \"spec\",\n    \"slug\": \"pose-review-readiness-before-seal\"\n  },\n  \"coordinator_relation\": \"same-project-authority\",\n  \"task_resolution\": {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n      \"kind\": \"spec\",\n      \"slug\": \"pose-review-readiness-before-seal\"\n    },\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution_state\": \"resolved\",\n    \"status\": \"in-progress\",\n    \"source_revision\": \"62a4e0f2730713ccd2913075ff980041c189f2c6\",\n    \"source_digest\": \"3c2f5491aa1692fea92279912edb722165863a59e0b681302d26608084a45736\"\n  },\n  \"authority_revision\": \"62a4e0f2730713ccd2913075ff980041c189f2c6\",\n  \"supported_contracts\": [\n    \"qualified-artifact-refs@1\",\n    \"spec-authority-transfer@1\",\n    \"federated-roadmap-acceptance@1\"\n  ],\n  \"context_revision\": \"4ffc11c71a05033e9a6ce7c743b0487b0b0a956b079be955d1cd62f5b95e13ae\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*backend-go*' -g '*knowledge-governance*'; git diff 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/cli\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*backend-go*' -g '*knowledge-governance*'; git diff 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/cli\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-23\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: \nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:review-readiness-before-seal\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nRefuse at seal, and let the reviewer check inside its run, every condition the conclusion preflight and `pose close` would otherwise refuse after a full review round.\n\n### Business value\nClosing `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks` took 23 review rounds. About seven were lost to conditions known before the reviewer started: a missing delivery declaration that `close` refused only after approval, a decision with no requirement basis, a finding id with a round prefix, `prior_findings` naming findings no concluded round holds open, criterion evidence outside the criterion's component, and a note file over 16 KiB. Each cost a seal, a delegated run and about 40 minutes.\n\n### Constraints\nThe checks reuse the existing preflight and closeout predicates; no rule is duplicated. A seal refusal names the rule and the fix. Nothing weakens a gate: what is refused later is refused earlier, never accepted.\n\n### Non-goals\nCapping review rounds, changing review independence, or judging the subject itself.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: `pose review bundle --seal` shall refuse a spec scope whose attributed changes touch a delivery root without a delivery declaration, with the same rule and message `pose close` uses (`undeclared-delivery`).\n- R2: When the plan asks for structural mappings, the seal shall refuse a spec scope with a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint, the rule the conclusion preflight applies to a mapping basis.\n- R3: A new `pose review draft-check <run|bundle> --draft <file>` shall run inside the review sandbox without writing. It reports every reason the conclusion preflight would refuse that draft: unreadable block, prefixed new finding ids, `prior_findings` outside the open findings, criterion evidence outside its component, undeclared decisions in mappings. It exits non-zero when any applies.\n- R4: The review brief shall instruct the reviewer to run `draft-check` on its draft before finishing, and list the open prior findings it must account for.\n- R5: `pose delegate` shall refuse a note file over the adapter limit with a message naming the note, its size and the limit, instead of the generic adapter-file error.\n- R6: When the instance has a conclusions issuer but the run is not concluded automatically, `pose delegate review` shall print the exact `pose review conclude <run>` command as the next step.\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual and its embedded copy.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:review-readiness-before-seal module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n\n### API/contract changes\nNew command `pose review draft-check`; new environment variable `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT` set for delegated review runs; new brief template `review-brief/8`; `review bundle --seal` refuses two more conditions for new seals.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nThe dispatch writes `pose-review-draft-context.json` to the run's private temporary directory; nothing is written to the repository.\n\n### Technical risks\nA draft check that drifted from the conclusion would mislead reviewers; it calls the same functions, and a test compares its reasons with the conclusion's refusal. Residual limits L1 and L2 are stated in the ADR.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [ ] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R3, R4\nThe draft check reuses the conclusion's parser, round accounting and attestation content checks, extracted as `attestationContentBlockers`, so it cannot accept what the conclusion refuses for content. It leaves out only the run's signature and identity, which do not exist before the run ends. See ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n### Decision D2\n- Basis: R1, R2\nThe seal applies only the readiness rules whose inputs exist before the review: the delivery declaration and the decision basis. Evidence and trace gates of `pose close` stay at close. A bundle already sealed is returned without being judged again.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-23: implemented R1–R6 with a regression test each, shown failing with its fix mutated out (seal refusal, decision basis, draft-check content, dispatch context, oversized note, conclude hint). `go test ./...` in `pose-mcp` passes.\n\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes. The canonical validation result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry` after the implementation commit.\n\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestSealRefusesAnUndeclaredDelivery\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestSealReadinessRefusesADecisionWithoutBasis\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewDraftCheckMatchesTheConclusionStep\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestTheCurrentBriefAsksForTheDraftCheck\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateNamesTheNoteLimitAndTheConclusionStep\n- R6 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateNamesTheNoteLimitAndTheConclusionStep\n\n\n### Known gaps\nThe draft check cannot run the signature and identity checks, which need the finished run; the conclusion step still runs them.\n\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe seal of a new spec bundle refuses an undeclared delivery and, when the plan asks for structural mappings, a decision basis that reaches no requirement. `pose review draft-check` reports what the conclusion step would refuse, inside the run, through a context the dispatch writes. The brief `review-brief/8` asks for it. `pose delegate` names an oversized note and the conclude command of a run nothing concluded.\n\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies, the ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 and L2 in the ADR: the draft check judges against the dispatch's context, and the seal reads the committed index.\n\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone.\n\n\n# ADR: Check review readiness before the seal and inside the run\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted on 2026-11-23 for `pose-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n## Context\n\nA delegated review round costs a seal, a run of about forty minutes and a conclusion. In the 23 rounds of `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks`, about seven were lost to refusals that existed before the reviewer started: `pose close` refused an approved scope for an undeclared delivery; the conclusion preflight refused drafts for a decision with no requirement basis, prefixed finding ids, prior findings outside the open ones, and criterion evidence outside its component. The reviewer could not see those rules applied to its own draft until the run had ended.\n\n## Decision\n\nMove each check to the earliest point that has its inputs, reusing the same predicate:\n\n- The seal of a new spec bundle refuses the `undeclared-delivery` finding the delivery index holds at error severity, the finding `pose close` reports. When the plan asks for structural mappings, it also refuses a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint, the namespace the preflight checks mappings against.\n- `pose review draft-check` runs the conclusion's draft parser, the round accounting and the attestation content checks over a draft, writing nothing. The content checks are the part of the bundle-attestation validation that does not depend on the run's signature or identity, extracted as one function both paths call.\n- A sealed checkout holds neither the bundle nor the run ledger, so the dispatch writes the bundle and the round's open findings to the run's private directory and names the file in `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT`. `--draft -` reads standard input for read-only sandboxes.\n- The brief of the new template `review-brief/8` asks the reviewer to run the check. Template texts are immutable, so `/7` stays for the runs briefed with it.\n\n## Consequences\n\nA scope that would fail at close now fails at seal, before any review cost. A reviewer can converge its draft inside one run. The draft check is advisory: the conclusion step stays the gate and still runs every check, including the signature and identity checks the draft check cannot run.\n\nResidual limits:\n- L1: the draft check judges against the context the dispatch wrote. A reviewer that edits that file only misleads itself, because the conclusion re-reads the sealed bundle and the ledger.\n- L2: the seal reads the delivery finding from the committed index. A stale index can miss a finding that a later `pose index` would add. `pose close` still refuses it, so the cost is a round, never a wrong closure.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- A per-instance cap on review rounds would stop the loop by approving unreviewed work.\n- Running the full `pose close` gate at seal would refuse scopes for evidence that only exists after the review.\nlocales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\nAGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\nindex 68bc3831..205aab97 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n@@ -454,6 +454,11 @@ func cmdDelegatePurpose(root, purpose string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.W\n \t}\n \tnotes := \"\"\n \tif f.noteFile != \"\" {\n+\t\t// R5 of spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal: an oversized note is\n+\t\t// named with its size and the limit, not as a generic adapter file.\n+\t\tif info, err := os.Lstat(f.noteFile); err == nil && info.Mode().IsRegular() && info.Size() > posemodel.ReviewNotesMaxBytes {\n+\t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, purpose, 1, fmt.Errorf(\"the note file %s has %d bytes; implementer notes must be at most %d bytes: shorten it\", f.noteFile, info.Size(), posemodel.ReviewNotesMaxBytes))\n+\t\t}\n \t\traw, err := posemodel.ReadReviewAdapterFile(f.noteFile, posemodel.ReviewNotesMaxBytes)\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, purpose, 1, err)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\nindex c6381d05..aed4adea 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n@@ -383,6 +383,7 @@ var commandHelpCatalog = map[string]CommandHelp{\n \t\t\t{\"bundle\", \"pose review bundle <scope|xref> [--seal] [--explain] [--expect-context <digest>]\", \"Prepare or seal an immutable review subject bundle\", \"Prepara ou sela o bundle imutável de revisão\"},\n \t\t\t{\"brief\", \"pose review brief <bundle-id|scope> [--kind review|adjudication|smoke] [--note-file <path>] [--json]\", \"Render the request a delegated reviewer receives, from the sealed bundle and, from round 2, the previous round's open findings\", \"Gera o pedido que um revisor delegado recebe, a partir do bundle selado e, da rodada 2 em diante, dos findings abertos da rodada anterior\"},\n \t\t\t{\"run-sign\", \"pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>] [--apply] [--json]\", \"Sign captured run provenance with a pinned native issuer\", \"Assina a proveniência capturada com issuer nativo fixado\"},\n+\t\t\t{\"draft-check\", \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\", \"Report every reason the conclusion step would refuse a review draft, without writing; inside a delegated review the bundle and round come from the run\", \"Relata todo motivo pelo qual a conclusão recusaria um rascunho de review, sem gravar; dentro de uma review delegada o bundle e a rodada vêm do run\"},\n \t\t\t{\"conclude\", \"pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]\", \"Record the typed conclusion of a completed delegated run: a review as its signed attestation, an adjudication on the spec, a smoke run as smoke evidence; or why it records none\", \"Registra a conclusão tipada de um run delegado concluído: uma review como atestação assinada, uma adjudicação na spec, um smoke como evidência smoke; ou por que não registra nenhuma\"},\n \t\t\t{\"request\", \"pose review request <scope|bundle-id> --kind delegated-review [--purpose review|adjudicate|smoke] [--agents <name,...>] [--note-file <path>] [--supersedes <act-id> [--authority <json>] [--role <role>] [--requested-at <time>]] [--apply] [--json]\", \"Open a delegated-review action request that a local run, a CI job or the Conductor fulfils\", \"Abre uma action request de review delegada que um run local, um job de CI ou o Conductor cumpre\"},\n \t\t\t{\"run-proof\", \"pose review run-proof <run-id> <proof-id> [--json]\", \"Verify current run proof and disclose executor assurance\", \"Verifica a prova atual e divulga assurance do executor\"},\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\nindex 22bfa902..973059fc 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n@@ -430,6 +430,8 @@ func cmdReview(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \t\treturn cmdReviewRunProof(root, args[1:], stdout, stderr)\n \tcase \"conclude\":\n \t\treturn cmdReviewConclude(root, args[1:], stdout, stderr)\n+\tcase \"draft-check\":\n+\t\treturn cmdReviewDraftCheck(root, args[1:], stdout, stderr)\n \tcase \"request\":\n \t\treturn cmdReviewRequest(root, args[1:], stdout, stderr)\n \t// The aliases pose-delegation-surface deprecated are removed (spec\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\nindex add10fc0..4fb97af5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n@@ -102,6 +102,11 @@ func delegateAutoConclude(store posemodel.Store, run posemodel.ReviewRun, err er\n \t\treturn\n \t}\n \tif conclusion == nil {\n+\t\t// R6 of spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal: a completed run that\n+\t\t// is not concluded automatically names the step that concludes it.\n+\t\tif next := delegateConcludeNextStep(store, run); next != \"\" {\n+\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Hint(next)\n+\t\t}\n \t\treturn\n \t}\n \tline := \"pose delegate: conclusion \" + conclusion.State\n@@ -113,3 +118,21 @@ func delegateAutoConclude(store posemodel.Store, run posemodel.ReviewRun, err er\n \t}\n \trender(stdout, stderr).Hint(line)\n }\n+\n+// delegateConcludeNextStep is the command that records the conclusion of a\n+// completed run nothing concluded, or \"\" when there is none to record.\n+func delegateConcludeNextStep(store posemodel.Store, run posemodel.ReviewRun) string {\n+\tif run.Status != posemodel.ReviewRunCompleted || run.RunID == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn \"\"\n+\t}\n+\tswitch run.Kind {\n+\tcase posemodel.ReviewBriefKindReview, posemodel.ReviewBriefKindAdjudication, posemodel.ReviewBriefKindSmoke:\n+\tdefault:\n+\t\treturn \"\"\n+\t}\n+\tcommand := \"pose review conclude \" + run.RunID\n+\tif policy, _, found, err := store.LoadDelegationPolicy(); err != nil || !found || policy.ConclusionsIssuer() == \"\" {\n+\t\tcommand += \" --issuer <name>\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"pose delegate: nothing concluded this run automatically; preview its conclusion with `\" + command + \"`, then record it with `\" + command + \" --apply`\"\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..30722b28\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"io\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n+)\n+\n+const reviewDraftCheckUsage = \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\"\n+\n+// cmdReviewDraftCheck reports the reasons a draft would be refused at\n+// conclusion, writing nothing (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3).\n+func cmdReviewDraftCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n+\tvar bundleID, draftPath string\n+\tjsonOut := false\n+\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n+\t\tswitch args[i] {\n+\t\tcase \"--json\":\n+\t\t\tjsonOut = true\n+\t\tcase \"--draft\":\n+\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) {\n+\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: --draft needs a file\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\ti++\n+\t\t\tdraftPath = args[i]\n+\t\tdefault:\n+\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[i], \"-\") || bundleID != \"\" {\n+\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: unexpected argument \"+args[i]+\"\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tbundleID = args[i]\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif draftPath == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the draft with --draft\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n+\t}\n+\tvar raw []byte\n+\tvar err error\n+\tif draftPath == \"-\" {\n+\t\traw, err = io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(os.Stdin, 4<<20))\n+\t} else {\n+\t\traw, err = os.ReadFile(draftPath)\n+\t}\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + err.Error())\n+\t\treturn 1\n+\t}\n+\tstore := cliGovernedStore(root)\n+\tvar reasons []string\n+\tcontextPath := os.Getenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv)\n+\tswitch {\n+\tcase bundleID == \"\" && contextPath == \"\":\n+\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the bundle; only a delegated review provides it\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n+\tcase contextPath != \"\" && bundleID == \"\":\n+\t\tctx, err := posemodel.ReadReviewDraftContext(contextPath)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n+\t\t\treturn 1\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treasons = store.CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx, string(raw), time.Now())\n+\tdefault:\n+\t\treasons, err = store.CheckReviewDraft(bundleID, string(raw), time.Now())\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n+\t\t\treturn 1\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif jsonOut {\n+\t\twriteJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"ok\": len(reasons) == 0, \"reasons\": nonNilStrings(reasons)})\n+\t} else if len(reasons) == 0 {\n+\t\trender(stdout, stderr).ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\")\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n+\t\tout.ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would refuse this draft:\")\n+\t\tfor _, r := range reasons {\n+\t\t\tout.ContractLine(\"  - \" + r)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif len(reasons) > 0 {\n+\t\treturn 1\n+\t}\n+\treturn 0\n+}\n+\n+func nonNilStrings(v []string) []string {\n+\tif v == nil {\n+\t\treturn []string{}\n+\t}\n+\treturn v\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..1439fd4a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3: draft-check reports what the\n+// conclusion step would refuse, before the run ends, and writes nothing.\n+func TestReviewDraftCheckMatchesTheConclusionStep(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcontextCopy := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"context.json\")\n+\troot, draftPath, bundleID := cliProvenanceInstance(t, func(root, draftPath string) {\n+\t\treviewers := posemodel.ReviewersPolicy{SchemaVersion: 1, Provenance: &posemodel.ReviewRunProvenancePolicy{Trust: \"executor-attested\", Implementation: posemodel.ModelIdentity{Principal: \"agent:implementer\", Execution: \"implementation-fixture\", Vendor: \"openai\", Model: \"implementation-model\"}}, Adapters: map[string]posemodel.ReviewerAdapter{\"fake\": {Executor: \"agent:reviewer\", Command: []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", \"cat >/dev/null; cp \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT\\\" '\" + contextCopy + \"'; cat '\" + draftPath + \"'\"}, Vendor: \"openai\", Model: \"review-model\"}}}\n+\t\traw, _ := json.Marshal(reviewers)\n+\t\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/policy/reviewers.json\", string(raw))\n+\t})\n+\ts := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\twriteRunConclusion(t, s, bundleID, draftPath)\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", bundleID, \"--draft\", draftPath); code != 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"would accept\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a draft the conclusion accepts was refused: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\n+\t// A criterion citing evidence the bundle did not seal, and a new finding\n+\t// carrying a round prefix: both refused, by the same words conclude uses.\n+\tgood, _ := os.ReadFile(draftPath)\n+\tbad := strings.Replace(string(good), \"integration:val-alpha\", \"integration:val-missing\", 1)\n+\tbadPath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"bad.txt\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(badPath, []byte(bad), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tcode, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", bundleID, \"--draft\", badPath, \"--json\")\n+\tvar report struct {\n+\t\tOK      bool     `json:\"ok\"`\n+\t\tReasons []string `json:\"reasons\"`\n+\t}\n+\tif code == 0 || json.Unmarshal([]byte(out), &report) != nil || report.OK || len(report.Reasons) == 0 || !strings.Contains(strings.Join(report.Reasons, \" \"), \"the attestation preflight refuses it\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a draft the preflight refuses passed the draft check: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\n+\t// Inside a delegated review, the run provides the bundle and the round.\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"review\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--agent\", \"fake\"); code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(code, out)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Stat(contextCopy); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the dispatch named no draft context: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tt.Setenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv, contextCopy)\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", \"--draft\", badPath); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"would refuse\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run's context did not judge the draft: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", \"--draft\", draftPath); code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run's context refused a good draft: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\t// From standard input, as a read-only sandbox can only offer it.\n+\tt.Setenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv, \"\")\n+\tstdin, _ := os.Open(badPath)\n+\tdefer stdin.Close()\n+\tsaved := os.Stdin\n+\tos.Stdin = stdin\n+\tcode, out = runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", bundleID, \"--draft\", \"-\")\n+\tos.Stdin = saved\n+\tif code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"would refuse\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a draft on standard input was not judged: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\t_ = time.Now\n+}\n+\n+// The same refusal at the conclusion step, so the check cannot drift from it.\n+func TestReviewDraftCheckRefusalIsTheConclusionRefusal(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, draftPath, bundleID := cliProvenanceInstance(t)\n+\ts := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\twriteRunConclusion(t, s, bundleID, draftPath)\n+\tgood, _ := os.ReadFile(draftPath)\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(draftPath, []byte(strings.Replace(string(good), \"integration:val-alpha\", \"integration:val-missing\", 1)), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\t_, checked := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", bundleID, \"--draft\", draftPath, \"--json\")\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"review\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--agent\", \"fake\"); code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(code, out)\n+\t}\n+\truns, _, _ := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n+\tcode, concluded := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"conclude\", runs[0].RunID, \"--issuer\", \"fixture-executor\", \"--apply\")\n+\tif code == 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"conclude accepted the draft: %s\", concluded)\n+\t}\n+\tvar report struct{ Reasons []string }\n+\t_ = json.Unmarshal([]byte(checked), &report)\n+\tfor _, r := range report.Reasons {\n+\t\tfor _, part := range strings.Split(strings.TrimPrefix(r, \"the attestation preflight refuses it: \"), \"; \") {\n+\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(concluded, part) {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"draft-check reported %q, which conclude did not: %s\", part, concluded)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R5, R6: an oversized note is named\n+// with its size and the limit; a completed run nothing concluded names the\n+// command that concludes it.\n+func TestDelegateNamesTheNoteLimitAndTheConclusionStep(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, draftPath, bundleID := cliProvenanceInstance(t)\n+\ts := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\twriteRunConclusion(t, s, bundleID, draftPath)\n+\tnote := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"note.md\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(note, []byte(strings.Repeat(\"n\", int(posemodel.ReviewNotesMaxBytes)+1)), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tcode, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"review\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--agent\", \"fake\", \"--note-file\", note)\n+\tif code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"implementer notes must be at most\") || !strings.Contains(out, note) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an oversized note was not named: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\tcode, out = runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"review\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--agent\", \"fake\")\n+\truns, _, _ := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n+\tif code != 0 || len(runs) != 1 || !strings.Contains(out, \"pose review conclude \"+runs[0].RunID+\" --issuer <name> --apply\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the conclusion step was not named: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..5aa4adf6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n+)\n+\n+// sealReadinessRoot is the dispatch fixture with the delivery policy enabled\n+// and the index holding the finding `pose close` would report, unsealed.\n+func sealReadinessRoot(t *testing.T, severity string) string {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\troot := newDetachedFixtureRoot(t)\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/policy/review.json\", `{\"schema_version\":2,\"enabled\":true,\"adopted_at\":\"2026-08-02\",\"profiles\":{\"spec\":\"spec-closeout@1\"},\"review_bundles\":true,\"review_bundles_adopted_at\":\"2026-08-14\"}`)\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/review-profiles/spec-closeout.json\", `{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"spec-closeout\",\"version\":1,\"scope\":\"spec\",\"criteria\":[{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"description\":\"reviewed\"}]}`)\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/policy/delivery.json\", `{\"schema_version\":1,\"enabled\":true,\"adopted_at\":\"2026-08-01\",\"results_path\":\".pose/results/current.json\",\"roots\":[{\"path\":\"pose-mcp\",\"kind\":\"capability\",\"profile\":\"api-contract\",\"entrypoint\":\"pose-mcp/lib.go\"}],\"severities\":{\"undeclared-delivery\":\"error\"}}`)\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/specs/alpha/spec.md\", \"---\\nslug: alpha\\nstatus: in-progress\\ncreated_at: 2026-08-02\\ncompleted_at:\\n---\\n\\n# Spec: alpha\\n\\n## 2. Requirements\\n- R1: works\\n\\n## 6. Validation\\n\\n### Requirement trace\\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestFixture\\n\")\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \"pose-mcp/lib.go\", \"package posemcp\\n\")\n+\tgit := func(args ...string) string {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tout, err := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\"}, args...)...).CombinedOutput()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tgit(\"add\", \"-A\")\n+\tgit(\"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"alpha\")\n+\thead := git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n+\tprovenance := \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"1\", 64)\n+\tgraph := posemodel.DeliveryIntegrityGraph{\n+\t\tSchemaVersion: 1, ProvenanceDigest: provenance,\n+\t\tChangeSets: []posemodel.ChangeSet{{ID: \"cs-alpha\", Spec: \"alpha\", Selector: \"range:\" + head + \"..\" + head, Base: head, Head: head, ResolvedBase: head, ResolvedHead: head,\n+\t\t\tPaths: []posemodel.ObservedPath{{Action: \"modified\", Path: \"pose-mcp/lib.go\"}}, DiffDigest: \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"2\", 64)}},\n+\t\tValidationResults: []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult{{ID: \"val-alpha\", Module: \"pose-mcp\", Check: \"go-test\", EvidenceClass: \"integration\", Severity: \"required\", Outcome: \"pass\", GitHead: head, ProvenanceDigest: provenance}},\n+\t\tReverse:           map[string][]string{\"pose-mcp/lib.go\": {\"alpha\"}},\n+\t\tFindings:          []posemodel.DeliveryIntegrityFinding{posemodel.NewDeliveryIntegrityFinding(\"undeclared-delivery\", severity, \"alpha\", \"pose-mcp/lib.go\", \"cs-alpha\", \"changed delivery root pose-mcp has no delivery declaration\", \"declare a typed delivery target or narrow the attributed change set\")},\n+\t}\n+\traw, _ := json.Marshal(graph)\n+\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \".pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json\", string(raw))\n+\treturn root\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R1: a spec scope whose change\n+// touches a delivery root without a declaration is refused at seal, with the\n+// rule `pose close` uses, instead of after an approved review.\n+func TestSealRefusesAnUndeclaredDelivery(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := sealReadinessRoot(t, \"error\")\n+\tcode, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"bundle\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--seal\")\n+\tif code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"undeclared-delivery [pose-mcp/lib.go]\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"pose close refuses it\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an undeclared delivery was sealed: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\t// A warning, as for a spec created before the delivery policy, seals.\n+\troot = sealReadinessRoot(t, \"warning\")\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"bundle\", \"spec:alpha\", \"--seal\"); code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a warning blocked the seal: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\nindex c77e594c..8ba600c5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n@@ -2134,6 +2134,9 @@ func (s Store) sealReviewBundle(ref string, identity *ReviewBundleImplementation\n \t\treplaced.Replaces = governing.BundleID\n \t\tidentity = &replaced\n \t}\n+\tif blockers := s.sealReadinessBlockers(bundle); len(blockers) > 0 {\n+\t\treturn bundle, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review bundle is not sealable: %s\", strings.Join(blockers, \"; \"))\n+\t}\n \t// A bundle already sealed reads as it was; a new seal holds a validation result,\n \t// whatever the lifecycle of the scope says.\n \tif !holdsValidationResult(bundle.Payload.Evidence) {\n@@ -3891,6 +3894,15 @@ func (s Store) validateBundleAttestationWith(bundle ReviewBundle, att ReviewAtte\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t}\n+\treturn append(blockers, s.attestationContentBlockers(bundle, att, skipEvidenceSupport)...)\n+}\n+\n+// attestationContentBlockers judges what an attestation says about its bundle,\n+// apart from who signed it: criteria, mappings, findings, evidence and tools.\n+// It is the part a reviewer's draft can be checked against before the run\n+// ends (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3).\n+func (s Store) attestationContentBlockers(bundle ReviewBundle, att ReviewAttestation, skipEvidenceSupport bool) []string {\n+\tblockers := []string{}\n \trequired := map[string]ReviewPlanCriterion{}\n \tfor _, criterion := range bundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria {\n \t\tif criterion.Required {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nindex ac0fc598..8542c982 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n@@ -965,6 +965,17 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t// The reviewer works in a sealed checkout: diagnostics it runs must not\n \t// publish derived records into it (SealedCheckoutEnv).\n \tenv = append(env, SealedCheckoutEnv+\"=\"+worktree)\n+\t// The reviewer checks its draft against the sealed bundle and the round\n+\t// before it finishes (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3). A\n+\t// context that cannot be built leaves the check unavailable, never the\n+\t// review.\n+\tif plan.Purpose == DelegationPurposeReview {\n+\t\tif draftCtx, err := s.ReviewDraftContextFor(plan.Bundle); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tif path, err := writeReviewDraftContext(tmp, draftCtx); err == nil {\n+\t\t\t\tenv = append(env, ReviewDraftContextEnv+\"=\"+path)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tcmd.Env = env\n \tcombined := &reviewBoundedCapture{limit: safety.StreamBytes, cancel: cancel}\n \tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = combined, combined\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..2b429d2b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+// Draft check (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3): the reasons the\n+// conclusion step and the attestation preflight would refuse a reviewer's\n+// draft, computed before the run ends and without writing anything. It\n+// reuses the same parsers and content checks; only the run's own proof,\n+// signature and identity, which do not exist yet, are left out.\n+//\n+// A sealed checkout holds the subject, not the bundle sealed over it nor the\n+// run ledger, so the dispatch writes both to the run's private directory and\n+// names it in ReviewDraftContextEnv.\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// ReviewDraftContextEnv names the file holding the bundle and round a draft\n+// is checked against inside a delegated review.\n+const ReviewDraftContextEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT\"\n+\n+const reviewDraftContextSchema = \"pose.review-draft-context/v1\"\n+\n+// ReviewDraftContext is what a draft is judged against: the sealed bundle and\n+// the findings its round must account for.\n+type ReviewDraftContext struct {\n+\tSchema string              `json:\"schema\"`\n+\tBundle ReviewBundle        `json:\"bundle\"`\n+\tRound  int                 `json:\"round\"`\n+\tOpen   []ReviewOpenFinding `json:\"open,omitempty\"`\n+}\n+\n+// ReviewDraftContextFor builds the context of bundle from the run ledger.\n+func (s Store) ReviewDraftContextFor(bundle ReviewBundle) (ReviewDraftContext, error) {\n+\tround, err := s.ReviewRoundOf(bundle)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ReviewDraftContext{}, err\n+\t}\n+\treturn ReviewDraftContext{Schema: reviewDraftContextSchema, Bundle: bundle, Round: round.Number, Open: round.Open}, nil\n+}\n+\n+// writeReviewDraftContext writes ctx under dir and returns its path.\n+func writeReviewDraftContext(dir string, ctx ReviewDraftContext) (string, error) {\n+\traw, err := json.Marshal(ctx)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn \"\", err\n+\t}\n+\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, \"pose-review-draft-context.json\")\n+\treturn path, os.WriteFile(path, raw, 0o600)\n+}\n+\n+// ReadReviewDraftContext reads a context file a dispatch wrote.\n+func ReadReviewDraftContext(path string) (ReviewDraftContext, error) {\n+\tvar ctx ReviewDraftContext\n+\traw, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ctx, err\n+\t}\n+\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &ctx); err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ctx, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: reading draft context %s: %w\", path, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif ctx.Schema != reviewDraftContextSchema || ctx.Bundle.BundleID == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn ctx, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %s is not a review draft context\", path)\n+\t}\n+\treturn ctx, nil\n+}\n+\n+// CheckReviewDraft returns every reason a draft for bundleID would be\n+// refused at conclusion, or nil when none applies.\n+func (s Store) CheckReviewDraft(bundleID, output string, now time.Time) ([]string, error) {\n+\tbundle, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(bundleID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, err\n+\t}\n+\tctx, err := s.ReviewDraftContextFor(bundle)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, err\n+\t}\n+\treturn s.CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx, output, now), nil\n+}\n+\n+// CheckReviewDraftIn judges output against ctx.\n+func (s Store) CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx ReviewDraftContext, output string, now time.Time) []string {\n+\tvar reasons []string\n+\tdraft, err := ParseReviewDraft(output)\n+\tswitch {\n+\tcase err != nil:\n+\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the conclusion cannot be read: \"+err.Error())\n+\tcase draft == nil:\n+\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the final message carries no pose-draft block\")\n+\t}\n+\tif err == nil {\n+\t\tround := ReviewRound{Number: ctx.Round, Open: ctx.Open}\n+\t\tif problems := ValidateRoundDraft(round, output); len(problems) > 0 {\n+\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the draft does not account for its round: \"+strings.Join(problems, \"; \"))\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif draft != nil && reviewDecisionApproves(draft.Decision) {\n+\t\tbundle := ctx.Bundle\n+\t\trun := ReviewRun{RunID: \"draft-check\", BundleID: bundle.BundleID, Kind: ReviewBriefKindReview}\n+\t\tatt := reviewAttestationFromDraft(run, bundle, *draft, \"agent:draft-check/unknown\")\n+\t\tcompleted, err := completeReviewAttestation(bundle, att, now)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the attestation preflight refuses it: \"+strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n+\t\t} else if blockers := s.attestationContentBlockers(bundle, completed, false); len(blockers) > 0 {\n+\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the attestation preflight refuses it: \"+strings.Join(uniqueSorted(blockers), \"; \"))\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn reasons\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..b9d2c1a0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+// Seal readiness (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R1, R2): a new seal\n+// refuses what `pose close` and the conclusion preflight would refuse only\n+// after a full review round, using the same rules. A bundle already sealed\n+// is returned as it was and never re-judged here.\n+\n+import \"sort\"\n+\n+func (s Store) sealReadinessBlockers(bundle ReviewBundle) []string {\n+\tscope, err := ParseScopeRef(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n+\tif err != nil || scope.Kind != \"spec\" {\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tvar blockers []string\n+\t// R1: the delivery declaration `pose close` requires, read from the same\n+\t// index findings the delivery assurance gate reports.\n+\tif policy, err := LoadDeliveryPolicyIn(s.fsys(), s.Root); err == nil && policy.Enabled {\n+\t\tif graph, err := s.GetDeliveryIntegrity(\"\"); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tfor _, finding := range graph.Findings {\n+\t\t\t\tif finding.Code != \"undeclared-delivery\" || finding.Spec != scope.Slug || finding.Severity != \"error\" && finding.Severity != \"critical\" {\n+\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tmsg := \"undeclared-delivery [\" + finding.Path + \"]: \" + finding.Message\n+\t\t\t\tif finding.Remediation != \"\" {\n+\t\t\t\t\tmsg += \" (\" + finding.Remediation + \")\"\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, msg+\"; pose close refuses it after the review\")\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// R2: a structural fact is mapped to a decision basis, and the preflight\n+\t// refuses a basis that reaches no requirement or constraint. When the plan\n+\t// asks for mappings, every declared decision must be usable as one.\n+\tif structure := bundle.Payload.Plan.Structure; structure != nil && len(structure.Material) > 0 {\n+\t\tns := s.reviewDesignBasisNamespace(scope)\n+\t\tvar unreached []string\n+\t\tfor id := range ns.Known {\n+\t\t\tif !ns.Reaches[id] {\n+\t\t\t\tunreached = append(unreached, id)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tsort.Strings(unreached)\n+\t\tfor _, id := range unreached {\n+\t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, \"decision basis \"+id+\" reaches no requirement or constraint: give it a `- Basis:` line naming one, or the conclusion preflight refuses a mapping to it\")\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn uniqueSorted(blockers)\n+}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go; sed -n '2000,2160p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; rg -n 'attestationContentBlockers|reviewDecisionApproves|completeReviewAttestation|ValidateRoundDraft|preflight' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclude.go; git diff 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go POSE.md; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go; sed -n '2000,2160p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; rg -n 'attestationContentBlockers|reviewDecisionApproves|completeReviewAttestation|ValidateRoundDraft|preflight' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclude.go; git diff 3f63a1bb..62a4e0f2 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go POSE.md; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md\"","aggregated_output":"package cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n)\n\nconst reviewDraftCheckUsage = \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\"\n\n// cmdReviewDraftCheck reports the reasons a draft would be refused at\n// conclusion, writing nothing (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3).\nfunc cmdReviewDraftCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\tvar bundleID, draftPath string\n\tjsonOut := false\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n\t\tswitch args[i] {\n\t\tcase \"--json\":\n\t\t\tjsonOut = true\n\t\tcase \"--draft\":\n\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) {\n\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: --draft needs a file\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tdraftPath = args[i]\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[i], \"-\") || bundleID != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: unexpected argument \"+args[i]+\"\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbundleID = args[i]\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif draftPath == \"\" {\n\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the draft with --draft\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t}\n\tvar raw []byte\n\tvar err error\n\tif draftPath == \"-\" {\n\t\traw, err = io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(os.Stdin, 4<<20))\n\t} else {\n\t\traw, err = os.ReadFile(draftPath)\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + err.Error())\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tstore := cliGovernedStore(root)\n\tvar reasons []string\n\tcontextPath := os.Getenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase bundleID == \"\" && contextPath == \"\":\n\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the bundle; only a delegated review provides it\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\tcase contextPath != \"\" && bundleID == \"\":\n\t\tctx, err := posemodel.ReadReviewDraftContext(contextPath)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\treasons = store.CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx, string(raw), time.Now())\n\tdefault:\n\t\treasons, err = store.CheckReviewDraft(bundleID, string(raw), time.Now())\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif jsonOut {\n\t\twriteJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"ok\": len(reasons) == 0, \"reasons\": nonNilStrings(reasons)})\n\t} else if len(reasons) == 0 {\n\t\trender(stdout, stderr).ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\tout.ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would refuse this draft:\")\n\t\tfor _, r := range reasons {\n\t\t\tout.ContractLine(\"  - \" + r)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(reasons) > 0 {\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\nfunc nonNilStrings(v []string) []string {\n\tif v == nil {\n\t\treturn []string{}\n\t}\n\treturn v\n}\n\t// like the refs it is computed from.\n\t//\n\t// Copied first: `canonical := payload` shares the slice backing array, so\n\t// clearing in place would erase the state on the bundle the caller is\n\t// holding, not on the copy being hashed.\n\tcanonical.Evidence = append([]ReviewBundleEvidence{}, canonical.Evidence...)\n\tfor i := range canonical.Evidence {\n\t\tcanonical.Evidence[i].SubjectObservation = \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn digestJSON(canonical)\n}\n\nfunc sortedBundleInputs(values []ReviewBundleInput) []ReviewBundleInput {\n\tresult := append([]ReviewBundleInput{}, values...)\n\tsort.Slice(result, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\treturn result[i].Kind+\"\\x00\"+result[i].Path+\"\\x00\"+result[i].Digest < result[j].Kind+\"\\x00\"+result[j].Path+\"\\x00\"+result[j].Digest\n\t})\n\treturn result\n}\n\nfunc normalizeBundleText(value string) string {\n\tlines := strings.Split(strings.ReplaceAll(value, \"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\"), \"\\n\")\n\tfor i := range lines {\n\t\tlines[i] = strings.TrimRight(lines[i], \" \\t\")\n\t}\n\treturn strings.TrimSpace(strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\"))\n}\n\nfunc digestText(value string) string { return digestBytes([]byte(normalizeBundleText(value))) }\nfunc digestBytes(value []byte) string {\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256(value)\n\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) reviewBundlesDir() string { return filepath.Join(s.Root, \".pose\", \"review-bundles\") }\nfunc (s Store) reviewAttestationsDir() string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(s.Root, \".pose\", \"review-attestations\")\n}\n\nfunc ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(files Files, root, rel string, create bool) (string, error) {\n\tclean, err := validateArtifactPathSyntax(rel)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tcurrent := root\n\tfor _, part := range strings.Split(filepath.Clean(clean), string(os.PathSeparator)) {\n\t\tcurrent = filepath.Join(current, part)\n\t\tinfo, statErr := files.Lstat(current)\n\t\tif os.IsNotExist(statErr) && create {\n\t\t\tif mkdirErr := files.Mkdir(current, 0o755); mkdirErr != nil && !os.IsExist(mkdirErr) {\n\t\t\t\treturn \"\", mkdirErr\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tinfo, statErr = files.Lstat(current)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif statErr != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", statErr\n\t\t}\n\t\tif info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n\t\t\trelPath, _ := filepath.Rel(root, current)\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: refusing to follow review artifact symlink at %s\", filepath.ToSlash(relPath))\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !info.IsDir() {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review artifact path is not a directory: %s\", filepath.ToSlash(rel))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn current, nil\n}\n\n// ensureReviewArtifactDir reads the filesystem directly; ensureReviewArtifactDirIn reads the operation's files.\nfunc ensureReviewArtifactDir(root, rel string, create bool) (string, error) {\n\treturn ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(NativeFiles(), root, rel, create)\n}\n\n// SealReviewBundle writes a prepared, unblocked bundle atomically. Replaying\n// the same payload is idempotent.\nfunc (s Store) SealReviewBundle(ref string, now time.Time) (ReviewBundle, error) {\n\treturn s.SealReviewBundleLead(ref, \"\", now)\n}\n\n// SealReviewBundleLead seals with the implementation identity lead declares,\n// or the one detected from the sealing session when lead is empty (spec\n// pose-delegation-routing R1–R3). Sealing content that a sealed bundle of the\n// scope already holds returns that bundle, which keeps the identity it was\n// sealed with: a reviewer resealing to close out never becomes the\n// implementation. Only a declared lead that names another identity seals anew.\nfunc (s Store) SealReviewBundleLead(ref, lead string, now time.Time) (ReviewBundle, error) {\n\tvar result ReviewBundle\n\terr := s.withReviewBundleWriteGuard(\"review.bundle.seal\", ref, func(guarded Store, _ ReviewBundle) error {\n\t\tvar err error\n\t\tresult, err = guarded.sealReviewBundleLead(ref, lead, now)\n\t\treturn err\n\t})\n\treturn result, err\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) sealReviewBundleLead(ref, lead string, now time.Time) (ReviewBundle, error) {\n\tidentity, warning, err := s.SealingIdentity(lead)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t}\n\tif identity.Vendor == ImplementationUnknown {\n\t\twarning = joinWarnings(warning, \"the seal records an unknown implementation vendor: no agent session was detected; seal from the implementing session or declare it with --lead\")\n\t} else if identity.ExecutionDigest == \"\" {\n\t\twarning = joinWarnings(warning, \"the seal names no implementation execution (no \"+identity.Vendor+\" session reference in the environment), so a review that must prove a different actor cannot be attested against it\")\n\t}\n\treturn s.sealReviewBundle(ref, &identity, lead != \"\", warning, now)\n}\n\n// sealReviewBundle seals ref recording identity; declared reseals content a\n// bundle already holds when that bundle records another identity. A nil\n// identity seals the way bundles were sealed before they recorded one, which\n// only the tests of the legacy reading need.\nfunc (s Store) sealReviewBundle(ref string, identity *ReviewBundleImplementation, declared bool, warning string, now time.Time) (ReviewBundle, error) {\n\tbundle, err := s.PrepareReviewBundle(ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t}\n\tif len(bundle.Blockers) > 0 {\n\t\treturn bundle, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review bundle is not sealable: %s\", strings.Join(bundle.Blockers, \"; \"))\n\t}\n\tsealed, err := s.ListReviewBundles(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t}\n\t// Content a sealed bundle already holds keeps the bundle that governs it,\n\t// unless a declared identity names another: then the new seal replaces\n\t// that bundle's identity by name, so it governs whatever the seal instants\n\t// say, and a historical identity declared again is a new seal, never the\n\t// historical bundle handed back (spec pose-delegation-routing D3).\n\tif governing := governingSealedBundle(sealed, bundle); governing != nil {\n\t\tif !declared || identity == nil || governing.Payload.Implementation != nil && sameImplementation(*governing.Payload.Implementation, *identity) {\n\t\t\treturn *governing, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treplaced := *identity\n\t\treplaced.Replaces = governing.BundleID\n\t\tidentity = &replaced\n\t}\n\tif blockers := s.sealReadinessBlockers(bundle); len(blockers) > 0 {\n\t\treturn bundle, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review bundle is not sealable: %s\", strings.Join(blockers, \"; \"))\n\t}\n\t// A bundle already sealed reads as it was; a new seal holds a validation result,\n\t// whatever the lifecycle of the scope says.\n\tif !holdsValidationResult(bundle.Payload.Evidence) {\n\t\tscope, err := ParseScopeRef(bundle.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tgraph, err := s.GetDeliveryIntegrity(\"\")\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif s.reviewScopeRequiresValidationEvidence(scope, bundle.Payload.Plan, graph) {\n\t\t\treturn bundle, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review bundle is not sealable: %s\", noValidationEvidenceBlocker)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif identity != nil {\n\t\tbundle.Payload.Implementation = identity\n\t\tdigest, err := reviewBundlePayloadDigest(bundle.Payload)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBundle{}, err\n\t\t}\nrg: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclude.go: IO error for operation on pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclude.go: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndiff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 3f2055de..f628d340 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -1071,7 +1071,9 @@ Preview `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>]`, then\n \n Attach `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` to a complete `pose review attest` request. The native issuer derives authority principal/execution bindings from the run and signs the exact reference. Criteria, tools, evidence and all ordinary preflight checks still apply. A rejecting or ambiguous draft cannot support an approval; a run-backed attestation cannot predate its completed run or signed proof. Adjudication/smoke run proofs bind their kinds but cannot be used as review attestations. Automatic validation/application of complete typed conclusions belongs to the capability, not to run signing.\n \n-**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/7` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole; a round after the first also names the findings it accounts for by the identifiers the brief lists, with their round, never a bare F1) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (low by default); any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` to `/7` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\n+**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/8` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole; a round after the first also names the findings it accounts for by the identifiers the brief lists, with their round, never a bare F1) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (low by default); any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` to `/8` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\n+\n+**Review readiness before the seal.** A new seal of a spec scope refuses what `pose close` and the conclusion preflight would otherwise refuse only after a full review round: a change to a delivery root with no delivery declaration (`undeclared-delivery`, read from the same index `pose close` reads), and, when the plan asks for structural mappings, a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint (give it a `- Basis:` line). A bundle already sealed is returned as it was. `pose review draft-check [<bundle-id>] --draft <file|-> [--json]` reports every reason the conclusion step would refuse a draft (an unreadable block, a round it does not account for, a criterion, mapping, finding, evidence or tool the attestation preflight refuses) and writes nothing; inside a delegated review the run provides the bundle and the round through `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT`, and `-` reads the draft from standard input, so it works in a read-only sandbox. The brief of template `review-brief/8` asks the reviewer to run it before finishing. `pose delegate` names an oversized note file with its size and the limit, and a completed run that nothing concluded automatically prints the `pose review conclude <run>` command that records it.\n \n **Delegated-review requests.** `pose review request <scope|bundle> --kind delegated-review [--purpose review|adjudicate|smoke] [--agents <name,...>] [--note-file <path>] [--apply]` opens an action request of kind `delegated-review` that binds the project, the worktree, the scope, the sealed bundle, the brief, the notes, the policies, the accepted agents and the destination of the conclusion (an attestation, an adjudication record or smoke evidence). No actor answers it: `pose action fulfil <act-id> --run <run-id> --runner agent:<id> --idempotency-key <key> --expected-revision <n> [--channel cli|ci|conductor] [--envelope <file>] [--apply]`, or the MCP tool `pose_action_fulfil`, submits a completed run, and the engine records the fulfilment only when the run is of the request's brief and bundle, of an accepted agent, completed with its containment, its signed proof verifies, its attempt ledger is intact and the engine recorded its conclusion at the request's destination; the fulfilment is verified again on every read. `pose delegate review <scope> --request <act-id>` runs the request's brief locally and submits the run once concluded. A rejecting run fulfils the request without approving anything; a superseded bundle or changed policy invalidates it, even once fulfilled, and it is asked again with `--supersedes <act-id>`, which retires it under the supersession authority rules (`--authority <json>`, `--role <role>`, `--requested-at` from the preview), or, when the plan now reserves the review for a person, makes the person's escalation its successor; a retry with the same key and run is a no-op. A person is asked by exception, as a decision request to the maintainer role: a plan that reserves the review for a person, a spent attempt budget, reviewers in conflict, and a `business_decision` a reviewer raised in its draft. A run's proof verifies in any checkout of the project: the worktree it ran in is recorded, not required of the reader, so a CI job or the Conductor fulfils the request with the same envelope.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\nindex 8b66ef79..82dd5e36 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ const (\n )\n \n var reviewBriefTemplates = map[string]string{\n-\tReviewBriefKindReview:       reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable,\n+\tReviewBriefKindReview:       reviewBriefTemplateDraftCheck,\n \tReviewBriefKindAdjudication: adjudicationBriefTemplateTyped,\n \tReviewBriefKindSmoke:        smokeBriefTemplateTyped,\n }\n@@ -65,6 +65,10 @@ const (\n \t// reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable is the current template: it also says that a draft\n \t// cannot dispense with every required criterion as not-applicable.\n \treviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable = \"review-brief/7\"\n+\t// reviewBriefTemplateDraftCheck is the current template: /7 plus the step\n+\t// that checks the draft with `pose review draft-check` before the run ends\n+\t// (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R4).\n+\treviewBriefTemplateDraftCheck = \"review-brief/8\"\n \t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions asked for the typed conclusion and stated its rules,\n \t// without the identifiers of the findings of earlier rounds.\n \t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions (/4) asked for the typed conclusion and stated the rules\n@@ -77,9 +81,15 @@ const (\n \treviewBriefTemplateFirst           = \"review-brief/1\"\n )\n \n+// reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable reports /7 and the templates that keep its\n+// text and add to it.\n+func reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template string) bool {\n+\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateDraftCheck\n+}\n+\n // reviewBriefAsksConclusion reports a template that asks for the typed conclusion.\n func reviewBriefAsksConclusion(template string) bool {\n-\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions || template == reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion\n+\treturn reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions || template == reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion\n }\n \n // briefRulesTextV5 is the statement of the rules the conclusion is checked against that\n@@ -91,7 +101,7 @@ const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and r\n // precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\n // evidence, and what a mapping's basis is.\n func briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n-\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules && template != reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n+\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules && !reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n \t\treturn briefRulesTextV5\n \t}\n \ttext := briefRulesTextV5\n@@ -101,7 +111,7 @@ func briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n \t}\n \ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\n \ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes;\", \"which is recorded as an accepted risk only when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (\"+severities+\"), or the draft requests changes and any finding of another severity is fixed first;\", 1)\n-\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n+\tif reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n \t\ttext += \" (l) a draft that dispenses with every required criterion as `not-applicable` is refused: a scope whose whole plan is inapplicable is not reviewed by it;\"\n \t}\n \treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\n@@ -110,14 +120,14 @@ func briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n // reviewBriefStatesRules reports a template that states the rules the conclusion is\n // checked against.\n func reviewBriefStatesRules(template string) bool {\n-\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions\n+\treturn reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions\n }\n \n // reviewBriefEarlierTemplates are the review templates a run may have been\n // briefed with before the current one, newest first; a run briefed with one\n // is re-rendered with it to verify and to continue (the brief a run was sent\n // never changes under it).\n-var reviewBriefEarlierTemplates = []string{reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules, reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs, reviewBriefTemplateConclusions, reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion, reviewBriefTemplateRounds, reviewBriefTemplateFirst}\n+var reviewBriefEarlierTemplates = []string{reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable, reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules, reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs, reviewBriefTemplateConclusions, reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion, reviewBriefTemplateRounds, reviewBriefTemplateFirst}\n \n // briefEarlierTemplates are, per kind, the templates a run may have been\n // briefed with before the current one, newest first.\n@@ -475,9 +485,12 @@ func renderReviewBriefBody(bundle ReviewBundle, kind, template, notes string, sm\n \t\t\tif reviewBriefStatesRules(template) {\n \t\t\t\tline(\"%d. %s\", next+2, briefRulesText(template, bundle))\n \t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateDraftCheck {\n+\t\t\t\tline(\"%d. Before you finish, check your final message: pipe it to `pose review draft-check --draft -` (it reads this run's bundle and round, writes nothing and works in a read-only sandbox) and fix every reason it reports. A draft it refuses is refused at conclusion, and the round is spent.\", next+3)\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t}\n-\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n+\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n \t\t// ParseReviewDraft refuses a draft whose `decision:` line outside the block disagrees\n \t\t// with the block, so the brief cannot say the outside is not read at all.\n \t\t// The last occurrence is the instruction of the step; an earlier one may be in the notes.\n@@ -495,7 +508,7 @@ func roundFields(round ReviewRound, template string) string {\n \tif round.Number < 2 {\n \t\treturn \"\"\n \t}\n-\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n+\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n \t\treturn \", `prior_findings` (each with `id`, `status` and `evidence`, one for every finding of the previous round; the `id` is the identifier listed under Findings to account for, which carries its round, for example R2-F1, never a bare F1, and a finding you report now takes an `id` that no earlier round used, for example N1: a bare or reused identifier makes the whole draft unreadable) and `sweep` (what you swept)\"\n \t}\n \treturn \", `prior_findings` (each with `id`, `status` and `evidence`, one for every finding of the previous round) and `sweep` (what you swept)\"\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
