{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s' 'decision: changes-requested\n\nThree medium-severity blockers: the seal gate exceeds R2'\\\\''s scope (N1), draft-check lacks R3'\\\\''s run-ID input (N2), and a missing artifact declaration blocks delivery verification (N3).\n\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-go and documentation-style rules. Focused regression tests and vet passed. Full canonical validation was not rerun in the read-only checkout; the broader Go test attempt exited 1, so no full-suite pass is claimed. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nBundle: rvb-0268e39f3711f7f3. Plan: sha256:3cfbd69688cfec3b0d559efebb47a313e9d6911bc210eafbbfc4f10ad7960edb.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"summary\": \"R2 applies only when the plan asks for structural mappings, but this condition checks only for material structural facts. ResolveReviewPlan observes structure before selecting overlays, so a structural selector that does not match can leave material facts without any required mapping criterion. Such a scope is now refused for an unrelated unbased decision although reviewStructuralCausalityBlockers returns immediately when there are no mapping owners. Gate this check on a required RequiresStructuralMapping criterion. The new TestSealReadinessRefusesADecisionWithoutBasis itself demonstrates the overreach by expecting blockers on a bundle with no criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\",\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"summary\": \"R3 requires draft-check <run|bundle>, but every positional argument is treated as a bundle ID and passed to LoadReviewBundle, which accepts only rvb-* IDs. Explicit run IDs always fail before checking the draft; they cannot recover the run'\"'\\\\''s bundle and round. Resolve a run reference to its bundle and round context, and cover that invocation. Reproduced with the source-built binary: draft-check run-fixture --draft - reports invalid review bundle id.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 67,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The artifact declaration omits modified pose-mcp/internal/pose/live_policy_reads_test.go. surface-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict reports error undeclared for that path, and the committed delivery-integrity index already contains the same scope-specific error. Declare its modified action and reconcile the attributed changes before closeout.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined D1/D2 and ADR limits L1/L2. Dispatch context is advisory and conclusion revalidates authority; stale delivery-index detection remains a documented limitation, not proof of readiness. Focused tests and vet were rerun; canonical validation is sealed evidence, not a fresh full validation run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected dispatch context creation before process start and existing temporary-directory lifecycle. No new shared mutable state or goroutines; existing writer coordination remains in place.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused DraftCheck, SealReadiness, SealRefuses and DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit tests passed. Inspected parser errors, schema checks and actionable seal/note diagnostics.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected CLI routing, dispatch environment/context and shared attestation-content extraction. Focused dispatch-context and conclusion-comparison regressions passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Returned reasons retain rule, path and remediation; note-limit errors name size and limit; conclude hints identify the run. Existing output containment/redaction remains unchanged.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 shares the parser, round accounting and content checks; D2 separates pre-review inputs from signature/identity checks and preserves existing-seal reuse. N1 violates D2'\\\\''s conditional scope.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-0bfbfab6\\\",\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR records R3/R4'\\\\''s shared content validation and private dispatch context; it also records D2'\\\\''s R1/R2 seal timing and residual limits L1/L2.\\\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed manual and scaffold diffs in both locales, /8 rendering and retained /7 text/digest. The docs match the implemented bundle/context CLI; N2 separately identifies its missing spec-required run form.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 and R4-R6 have exercised regressions; R2 is overbroad (N1), R3 omits run-ID input (N2), and the artifact gate remains blocked (N3).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation follows the planned module and delivery, but its artifact claims omit one changed test and R2 expands enforcement beyond the specified precondition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined private 0600 context publication, existing adapter confinement and final authority checks. Editing the advisory context cannot authorize an attestation. No new credential handling or authority bypass found.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Extracting existing content validation and passing a private snapshot is a small sufficient solution for an offline sealed checkout. It avoids a second validation engine and premature closeout. Signature/identity stay deferred. A mutable authority context would invalidate the choice. Cheapest formal shortcuts are editing the advisory context or giving a decision an arbitrary valid Basis; conclusion revalidation protects authority, while substantive causality remains reviewer judgment. No dedicated new readiness case exists in the adversarial corpus; focused refusal tests provide narrower coverage.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; artifact reconciliation reports undeclared live_policy_reads_test.go, also independently present in the committed delivery-integrity findings (N3).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded from this sealed read-only run. Inspected sealed structure:design-179046b00fd968e0 and mapped its governance delta.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Do not publish assessment artifacts into the sealed checkout; inspected component source and regression tests directly.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Inspected CLI/dispatch/conclusion boundaries and sealed integration evidence instead.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Searched the new readiness/draft-check files directly for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic; none found.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this review; no attestation was recorded by the reviewer.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this review; no attestation was recorded by the reviewer.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; applied security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Sealed integration evidence inspected, but independent pose surface-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict returned an undeclared-artifact error for live_policy_reads_test.go (N3).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Full pose validate was not rerun because registered checks can write in the sealed checkout. Used sealed canonical build/unit/integration/e2e evidence and independently reran focused Go tests and vet. The broader go test ./... attempt ended with exit 1; CLI tests passed in 203.813s, but no full-suite pass is claimed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Same read-only validation limitation. Focused go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\\''DraftCheck|SealReadiness|SealRefuses|DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit|Brief|SealedGate|OnlyTheSigning'\\\\'' and go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/pose ./internal/cli passed; unit:pose-mcp/go/test is sealed canonical evidence.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```'\"' | /home/go/.cache/go-build/ee/eefec43593745dd8d859745f1c289f8ebff6f551eaaf37a8a51763e72e617d86-d/pose review draft-check --draft -\"","aggregated_output":"Usage: pose review <bundle|brief|attest|auto-attest|verify|record|attribution-supplement> ...\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
