{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThree medium-severity blockers: R2’s seal gate applies beyond its specified scope, R3’s run-ID input is missing, and an undeclared artifact blocks delivery verification.\n\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-go, and documentation-style rules. Focused regression tests and vet passed. The broader Go test attempt exited 1; no full-suite pass is claimed.\n\nFinal draft validation remains unavailable: the installed binary lacks `draft-check`, the temporary source-built binary was cleaned up, and rebuilding was refused by the read-only filesystem. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nBundle: `rvb-0268e39f3711f7f3`. Plan: `sha256:3cfbd69688cfec3b0d559efebb47a313e9d6911bc210eafbbfc4f10ad7960edb`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"summary\": \"R2 applies only when the plan asks for structural mappings, but this condition checks only for material structural facts. Review-plan resolution observes structure before selecting overlays, so a nonmatching structural selector can leave material facts without a required mapping criterion. Such scopes are now refused for unbased decisions although reviewStructuralCausalityBlockers returns immediately without mapping owners. Gate readiness on a required RequiresStructuralMapping criterion. TestSealReadinessRefusesADecisionWithoutBasis demonstrates the overreach by expecting blockers from a bundle with no criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\",\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"summary\": \"R3 requires draft-check <run|bundle>, but every positional argument is passed as a bundle ID to LoadReviewBundle, which accepts only rvb-* IDs. Run IDs therefore always fail before draft validation and cannot select their recorded bundle and round. Resolve run references explicitly and test that invocation. The source-built binary reproduced the bundle-ID rejection for draft-check run-fixture --draft -.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\",\n      \"line\": 67,\n      \"summary\": \"The artifact declarations omit modified pose-mcp/internal/pose/live_policy_reads_test.go. The independent strict surface check reports error undeclared for that path, and the committed delivery-integrity index contains the same scope-specific error. Declare its modified action and reconcile the attributed changes before closeout.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined D1/D2 and ADR limits L1/L2. Dispatch context is advisory; conclusion revalidates authority. A stale delivery index remains a documented detection limitation. Focused tests and vet were independently rerun; canonical validation remains sealed evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected context publication before process start and the existing temporary-directory lifecycle. No new shared mutable state or goroutines were introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused DraftCheck, SealReadiness, SealRefuses and note-limit tests passed. Inspected parser errors, context schema checks and actionable readiness diagnostics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected CLI routing, dispatch context and shared attestation-content extraction. Focused context and conclusion-comparison regressions passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Returned errors retain rule, path and remediation. Note errors name size and limit; conclusion hints identify the run. Existing output containment remains intact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 shares parsing, round accounting and content validation. D2 separates pre-review readiness from final authority checks, but N1 violates its conditional scope.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-0bfbfab6\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records R3/R4's shared validation and private dispatch context, together with D2's seal timing and residual limits.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed manual and scaffold changes in both locales, /8 rendering and preservation of /7 text and digest. Documentation describes the implemented bundle/context command; N2 separately identifies the missing spec-required run form.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 and R4-R6 have exercised regressions. R2 is overbroad under N1, R3 omits run-ID input under N2, and artifact reconciliation remains blocked under N3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Implementation stays within the planned component, but artifact declarations omit a changed test and readiness enforcement exceeds R2's stated precondition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined private 0600 context publication, adapter confinement and final authority checks. Editing advisory context cannot authorize an attestation. No new credential exposure or authority bypass was found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Extracting existing validation and passing a private snapshot is a small sufficient solution for a sealed checkout. Signature and identity checks remain deferred. Mutable authoritative context would invalidate this choice. Editing advisory context or supplying an arbitrary valid Basis are cheap formal shortcuts: conclusion revalidation protects authority, while substantive causality remains reviewer judgment. No dedicated readiness case exists in the adversarial corpus; focused refusal tests provide narrower coverage.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed. Reconciliation identifies undeclared live_policy_reads_test.go, independently corroborated by the committed delivery-integrity finding N3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment writers were excluded from the sealed checkout. Inspected sealed structure evidence and mapped the governance delta.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided assessment publication into the sealed checkout; inspected component source and regressions directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment writers were excluded. Inspected CLI, dispatch and conclusion boundaries and sealed integration evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment writers were excluded. Direct searches of the new readiness and draft-check files found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires completion and recording of this review; the reviewer recorded no attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires completion and recording of this review; the reviewer recorded no attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed; applied security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected sealed evidence. Independently executed pose surface-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict, which reported the undeclared artifact in N3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Full pose validate was not rerun because registered checks can write in the sealed checkout. Used sealed canonical evidence and independently reran focused tests and vet. The broader go test ./... attempt exited 1; CLI tests passed in 203.813s, but no full-suite pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Read-only validation limitation. Focused go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'DraftCheck|SealReadiness|SealRefuses|DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit|Brief|SealedGate|OnlyTheSigning' and go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/pose ./internal/cli passed. unit:pose-mcp/go/test remains sealed canonical evidence.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
